<title>FRANCE: French car exports up 11.8 pct in January.</title>
<headline>French car exports up 11.8 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of French cars rose 11.8 percent in January to 193,585 units, the French carmakers' association CCFA said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Production rose 0.6 percent to 270,525 in the same month as the rise in exports helped offset a 33.7 percent plunge in domestic car sales to 122,320 units.</p>
<p>Exports by the PSA Peugeot Citroen rose 26.5 percent to 152,879. Renault exports fell 2.9 percent to 115,681, the CCFA said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
